I haven't used PGP for years, but I thought it worked by a web of
trust.  I.e. people sign each other's PGP public keys to verify that
this key belongs to the person who claims to own it.  The signed keys
are then put up on a public keyserver.  If you found the original
poster's key on there, and it was signed by someone you knew and
trusted, that would be some guarantee of their identity.  If not,
perhaps you could still find a chain of signatures that led back to
someone you knew and trusted.
